\pard\sa200\fs22 Hi Storyteller team,\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 I'm applying for your Junior/Graduate Software Engineer role, and the part of your posting about being AI-native - both in the product and in how you build - is exactly what made me want to write.\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 I'm a junior full-stack developer who learns and ships by building real things. I founded AfriCarbon, a charcoal business in Liberia, and built its entire software stack myself: a customer-facing storefront and Charcoal Manager, a production, sales, and profit tracking system the business runs on every day. It's an installable, mobile-first PWA with authentication, a Supabase/PostgreSQL backend, and a React and TypeScript frontend on Vercel - designed, built, tested, and deployed end to end, solo.\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 AI-assisted coding isn't a buzzword for me; it's how I work. I use code assistants to move quickly, but I treat their output as a draft to be checked - verifying with tests and reasoning from first principles before anything ships. That's exactly what your take-home describes, and it's the working style I'm most excited to bring to a product team.\par
\pard\sa200\fs22 I know I'm early in my career and haven't built SDKs yet, but I pick things up fast, I follow through, and I'm genuinely eager to grow into the iOS, Android, and Web work you do. I'd love the chance to talk about how I could contribute.\par
\pard\sa40\fs22 Thanks for your time,\par
\pard\sa0\fs22{\b Sylvester McDaniel Kollie}\par
